WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.830
John: Good morning, Hank, so here's how the
Paper Towns tour went.

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:05.830
I said goodbye to my beloved vacation hammock
and also my beloved family, and then drove

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:09.130
across Michigan to Lansing, blasting The Mountain
Goats the whole way.

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:13.110
Stopped only once on the drive, peemergency,
then I was in the airport, and then on a plane,

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:16.670
and then I was driving through New York City
watching the sun set behind the skyline.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:20.640
My hotel room was fancy, but I couldn't sleep,
so I woke up groggy, ironed clothes, brushed

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.039
teeth, got dressed, and met up with my friend
and publicist Elyse Marshall, and then headed

00:00:24.039 --> 00:00:26.040
over to the YouTube Space to meet Nat.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.040
Nat: John!

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.789
John: We collabed with The Gregory Brothers,
and then did an interview with The Young Turks,

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:33.010
where one of the interviewers was wearing
a pink shirt with a green dragon breathing

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:37.000
orange fire, like Young Margo does in Paper
Towns, and my life felt weird.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.860
Paper Towns is about the challenge of understanding
that other people are as complex as you are,

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.510
which is very hard for anyone, but especially
for anyone living inside this weird publicity

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:49.649
machine, because it does ultimately sort of
commodify everyone it touches, and I was thinking

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:53.649
about that as I saw two-dimensional images
of my friends, or possibly my characters,

00:00:53.649 --> 00:00:55.030
plastered all over New York City.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:58.250
Anyway, got some lunch for my publisher, Julie
Strauss-Gabel, who has on her wall the first

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:02.239
map ever made containing Agloe, NY, and we
talked about how much she liked the movie,

00:01:02.239 --> 00:01:05.630
and then I had to go to Burbury to get a suit
for next week's premiere and on the way, I

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:08.959
confessed to Elyse that I was a little bit
tired, and she pointed out that technically,

00:01:08.959 --> 00:01:10.719
the tour had not yet begun.

00:01:10.719 --> 00:01:14.560
Flew to Indianapolis and drove through my
hometown before experiencing the unspeakable

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:16.909
luxury of sleeping in my own bed.

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:20.200
The next morning, I discovered a trove of
clean pants, which never happens even at the

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.270
fanciest hotels.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:25.189
Then I met up with Halston Sage and Nat and
we did interviews and interviews and interviews,

00:01:25.189 --> 00:01:26.740
before heading over to the Murat theater.

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:30.380
I signed books for a while in a suit that
I only now realize was quite wrinkly, and

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:34.590
then there were more interviews and more interviews
and then, once I was good and sweaty, I got

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:36.279
my picture taken with Nat and Halston.

00:01:36.279 --> 00:01:37.279
Then the show started.

00:01:37.279 --> 00:01:40.919
Nat and his brother Alex played some songs
together, and I love both those guys so much,

00:01:40.919 --> 00:01:44.679
and I love watching them play music together,
because it reminds me of my own relationship

00:01:44.679 --> 00:01:48.579
with my brother, except for the part about
how Hank refuses to let me into his band,

00:01:48.579 --> 00:01:50.680
simply because I cannot sing or play any instruments.

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:54.659
Then I went out on stage with our great host,
Akilah Hughes, and I felt this immense wave

00:01:54.659 --> 00:01:59.680
of energy and then the mayor of Indianapolis
came out and declared July 14th, 2015 to be

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.679
John Green Day, which, you know, very weird,
and afterwards, I got to meet Anthony and

00:02:04.679 --> 00:02:08.640
Jack from the Indianapolis Colts, and then
everyone was feeling pretty good and we flew

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.650
to Columbus, and I got to have a drink with
Akilah, and then I went to bed.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.730
I'm not sure why I videotaped every bed on
tour.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:16.319
I think I was just excited about the prospect
of sleeping.

00:02:16.319 --> 00:02:19.489
Woke up a couple hours later just a smidge
tired, but the car taking me to interviews

00:02:19.489 --> 00:02:21.989
had ice cold Coke Zero in it, so that was
nice.

00:02:21.989 --> 00:02:25.650
Met up with Cara and Cara tried to adopt this
mongoose-like thing named Sherman, and then

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:29.410
we did a TV interview where Cara reluctantly
beatboxed, and I was told that the anchors

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:31.439
really liked my book, No Fault in These Stars.

00:02:31.439 --> 00:02:34.450
Then we did some more interviews and then
back at the hotel, I signed some books, and

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:37.840
then went to the theater, where we got to
sign for fans for a while, and then there

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:41.310
were interviews and interviews and interviews
until I was good and sweaty, which meant it

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:42.310
was time to be photographed.

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:45.870
The crowd in Columbus was amazing and asked
great questions and I kept thinking about

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:50.470
how long ago my college days in Ohio felt,
but before I could get properly nostalgic,

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.730
we were yanked away to the airport on a flight
to Dallas.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:56.540
The next morning, I got dressed, brushed my
teeth, and found Nat and Halston atop a balcony.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:57.709
God, I love those guys.

00:02:57.709 --> 00:03:00.900
Then I got my makeup done, and then interviews
and interviews and interviews.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:04.579
Went to my room to sign some more books and
then headed over to the theater where Dallas

00:03:04.579 --> 00:03:05.579
was hot.

00:03:05.579 --> 00:03:08.520
Now, I didn't have a thermometer with me,
but I think it was in the neighborhood of

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.530
15.7 million degrees Kelvin.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:13.769
Fortunately, because she is a good friend,
Elyse was kind enough not to videotape me

00:03:13.769 --> 00:03:17.750
getting photographed while my face melted
from the heat, but then, after just two changes

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:21.720
of shirts, I was able to meet our hosts, Gabby
and Allison from Just Between Us, and then

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:25.940
listened to Saint Motel, and finally meet
the amazing crowd in Dallas who were just

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:29.939
awesome, and then suddenly, it was over, and
we were on a plane to LA.

00:03:29.939 --> 00:03:33.329
Hank, the Paper Towns movie is out in most
of the world now, and I'm so grateful to everyone

00:03:33.329 --> 00:03:37.730
who has watched it and shared their responses
via nerdfighteria's #wallofcow.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:40.049
It's been a long and difficult two months
for me.

00:03:40.049 --> 00:03:44.430
I've missed my family a lot and I'm so glad
to be home with them now, but what an adventure

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:49.599
that week was, and like the best adventures,
it brought me closer to people I love, so

00:03:49.599 --> 00:03:51.959
thanks to all of them, and to everyone who
made the movie.

00:03:51.959 --> 00:03:57.000
Hank, thank YOU for a great VidCon, I am now
going to sleep until Friday, I will see you

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:57.019
then.

